# ReRoute backend process definitions for Render and Railway.
#
# The installed distribution is `reroute-backend` (see backend/pyproject.toml)
# and it ships the `app` package, so the ASGI application is importable as
# `app.main:app` from the repository `backend/` directory. `--host 0.0.0.0` and
# `--port $PORT` are required because the platform injects the bind port as an
# environment variable.
#
# One worker on purpose: the orchestration run is an in-process asyncio task and
# the WebSocket connection registry is in-process state, so a second worker would
# not see the first worker's sockets or orchestration. Scale with more instances
# and a shared store instead, not with `--workers`.
#
# No `release:` command is defined. There is no migration tool in this repository
# and no migration step to run: the SQLite session store creates its own schema
# with `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` during application startup, so `web:` is the
# only process the service needs.
web: uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT
